From: liujixings <liujixings@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: register bridge multicast groups with the PPE

Mirror the bridge IGMP/MLD snooping MDB into the PPE L2B multicast
entries on AN7581:

- Register a switchdev blocking notifier and translate port MDB add/del
  events into the PPE egress port mask for GDM1..GDM4.
- Keep a per-(eth, VID, MAC) registry so multiple bridge ports can join
  the same group. Only update entries the hardware has already learned;
  groups that cannot be derived from an IP multicast address are ignored.
- Retry every second while the L2B entry is still missing, since the PPE
  creates it on the first multicast packet, and invalidate only the
  affected entry when the last port leaves the group.
- Export airoha_netdev_to_gdm_dev() to safely resolve driver-owned
  netdevs, and add /sys/kernel/debug/ppe/multicast with the registry and
  counters.
- Resolve DSA user ports through dsa_port_from_netdev() and
  dsa_port_to_conduit(): the group is fanned out on the conduit GDM
  bit, and the last hop is left to the mt7530 MDB/flooding.

Signed-off-by: liujixings <liujixings@outlook.com>
